From d89d7d622d2c9e21a670904aeee90a7369d55c5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:34:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vibrator: Support the si_haptic input device

Xiaomi onyx uses a SiliconHaptic sih688x that registers as si_haptic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 aidl/Vibrator.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aidl/Vibrator.cpp b/aidl/Vibrator.cpp
index 8421cbf..5e4b8a2 100644
--- a/aidl/Vibrator.cpp
+++ b/aidl/Vibrator.cpp
@@ -142,7 +142,8 @@ InputFFDevice::InputFFDevice()
                 && strcmp(name, "aw8695_haptic")
                 && strcmp(name, "aw8697_haptic")
                 && strcmp(name, "awinic_haptic")
-                && strcmp(name, "drv2624:haptics")) {
+                && strcmp(name, "drv2624:haptics")
+                && strcmp(name, "si_haptic")) {
             ALOGD("not a supported haptics device\n");
             close(fd);
             continue;
-- 
2.43.0

